From ec9a301c7d333b8de33346fddf901fccc800e331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BrLumen <igflocal@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:57:23 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows: Do not skip the port's own node when it is the
 composite parent

get_port_details() builds the USB path of a port from the CM_DRP_ADDRESS
of every USB layer above it, and skips one layer for composite devices
because the child nodes usbccgp creates for the interfaces carry the
same address as the composite parent.

The check looks at the compatible IDs of the node, which advertise
USB\COMPOSITE for any device with bDeviceClass = 0 -- also when no
usbccgp is involved at all because a driver was bound to the whole
device.  That is what happens for a CDC device without an interface
association descriptor once usbser.sys is attached by VID/PID: the port
node itself is the composite-capable device, it gets skipped, the path
ends up empty and sp_get_port_usb_vid_pid() and friends report
SP_ERR_SUPP although the port is plainly USB.

Only skip a composite node that is a parent of the port's node; the
port's own node is the first layer and must contribute its address.

Signed-off-by: BrLumen <igflocal@gmail.com>
---
 windows.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/windows.c b/windows.c
index 2825a92..e6c0801 100644
--- a/windows.c
+++ b/windows.c
@@ -428,10 +428,20 @@ SP_PRIV enum sp_return get_port_details(struct sp_port *port)
 				    || strncmp(device_id, "USB\\", 4))
 					continue;
 
-				/* Discard one layer for composite devices. */
+				/*
+				 * Discard one layer for composite devices: the child
+				 * nodes usbccgp creates for the interfaces carry the
+				 * same address as the composite parent, so the parent
+				 * must not add it a second time. The port's own node
+				 * is exempt: when the serial driver is bound to the
+				 * whole device (e.g. usbser on a CDC device without
+				 * an interface association descriptor) there is no
+				 * child layer that could have contributed the address.
+				 */
 				char compat_ids[512], *p = compat_ids;
 				size = sizeof(compat_ids);
-				if (CM_Get_DevNode_Registry_PropertyA(dev_inst,
+				if (dev_inst != device_info_data.DevInst &&
+				    CM_Get_DevNode_Registry_PropertyA(dev_inst,
 				                                      CM_DRP_COMPATIBLEIDS, 0,
 				                                      &compat_ids,
 				                                      &size, 0) == CR_SUCCESS) {
-- 
